## Template only — deploy.sh writes the REAL infra/vps/caddy/active/api.caddy
## on the VPS (gitignored, never committed; not synced by rsync — see
## .gitignore and the rsync --exclude in cd.yml). Copy this file by hand only
## for the very first `deploy.sh --bootstrap` run on a fresh VPS, so Caddy has
## something importable before any deploy has ever run.
##
## Steady state (100% of traffic on one color) looks like this:
reverse_proxy api-blue:3000 {
	health_uri /api/health
	health_interval 10s
	health_timeout 5s
}

## During a canary window (deploy.sh phase 10), the same file instead holds a
## weighted two-upstream block, e.g. 90/10 in favor of the previously-live
## color while the candidate proves itself against a slice of real traffic:
##
## reverse_proxy api-blue:3000 api-green:3000 {
## 	lb_policy weighted_round_robin 9 1
## 	health_uri /api/health
## 	health_interval 10s
## 	health_timeout 5s
## }
##
## Both shapes are swapped in via temp-file-plus-`mv` (atomic) followed by
## `docker compose exec caddy caddy reload --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
## --adapter caddyfile` — no restart, no port rebind, in-flight requests
## finish against their original upstream.
